  "title": "Erdős Problem #102",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $c>0$ and $h_c(n)$ be such that for any $n$ points in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ such that there are $\\geq cn^2$ lines each containing more than three points, there must be some line containing $h_c(n)$ many points. Estimate $h_c(n)$. Is it true that, for fixed $c>0$, we have $h_c(n)\\to \\infty$?",
